  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be the function defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8469;</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></msubsup><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
